# Delta Sort Performance Regression — Fix Report

## Bug

In b35.2.0, the CSRM pipeline refactor removed `createChangePath()` and replaced it with `ensureRowsPath()`, which only creates a `ChangedPath` for hierarchical (grouped/tree) grids. For flat grids, `changedPath` is now `undefined`.

In `deltaSort.ts`, the row classification condition was:

```ts
if (updates.has(node) || adds.has(node) || !changedPath || changedPath.hasRow(node))
```

When `changedPath` is `undefined`, `!changedPath` evaluates to `true` — marking **all 100k nodes as "touched"**, which degenerates delta sort into a full sort.

## Fix

One-character change in `deltaSort.ts:65` — use optional chaining:

```ts
if (updates.has(node) || adds.has(node) || changedPath?.hasRow(node))
```

When `changedPath` is `undefined` (flat grids), `changedPath?.hasRow(node)` returns `undefined` (falsy), so only actual adds/updates are marked as touched.

## Benchmark Results

`applyTransaction` with 1 add + 1 update on 100k rows, 3-column descending sort new benchmark created in this PR:

| Version                  | deltaSort: true | deltaSort: false | Delta speedup |
| ------------------------ | --------------- | ---------------- | ------------- |
| **b35.1.0** (baseline)   | 85 ms           | 697 ms           | 8.2x faster   |
| **b35.2.0** (regression) | 410 ms          | 404 ms           | 1.0x (broken) |
| **b35.2.0 + fix**        | 78 ms           | 396 ms           | 5.1x faster   |

The regression is resolved.

For normal transactions, Version 35.2.0 is **1.7x** fater than version 35.1.0 because the recent improvements in ChangedPath in this release.

For delta sorting and transactions the speed is almost identical, slightly faster.

## Key Observations

-   **Regression confirmed**: In b35.2.0, delta sort was identical speed to full sort (~410 ms vs ~404 ms)
-   **Fix restores delta sort**: 78 ms with fix vs 85 ms on b35.1.0 — slightly faster due to other pipeline improvements
-   **Full sort improved in b35.2.0**: 396 ms vs 697 ms — the CSRM pipeline refactor improved the non-delta path by ~43%
-   **No risk to full refreshes**: `doDeltaSort` is only called when `changedRowNodes` is defined (transaction paths only). Non-transaction refreshes (sort/filter changes, `setRowData` without `getRowId`) always use full sort — completely unaffected by this change.
